<title>USA: TVA 1,148 MW nuke shuts for planned refuel.</title>
<headline>TVA 1,148 MW nuke shuts for planned refuel.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear's 1,148 megawatt Sequoyah nuclear power unit 1 has been shut for an estimated 45 days of scheduled maintenance and refueling, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Soddy-Daisy, Tenn., shut Friday and has been tentatively been set to return to service on May 9, the NRC said in its daily plant status report for Monday.</p>
<p>The adjoining 1,148 megawatt Sequoyah 2 nuclear power unit continued to operate normally at full capacity as of early Monday, the NRC said.</p>
<p>TVA Nuclear is a subsidiary of Tennessee Valley Authority.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
